r. Invoice wording and invoicing company to confirm.","signoff":true,"when":{"origin":["UK"],"destZone":["EU","NL"],"type":["B2C"],"value":["high"]},"then":{"warning":"Ship from EU stock if you can. Above €150 IOSS can''t be used, so import VAT ({destRate}) and any duty are collected at the border unless you ship duties paid (DDP).","needsVat":false,"level":"warn","entity":"NL","code":"0% UK Export","rate":{"kind":"fixed","value":0},"invoice":"Zero-Rated UK Export. Import VAT and duty are payable on import into {dest}."}},{"id":"r-nl-rc","name":"NL stock to a business, delivered in NL","note":"Differs from spreadsheet v3: its formula skips the reverse charge when goods ship from the Netherlands and gives intra-community supply or triangulation. Miranda confirmed (13 Oct) the reverse charge applies to any business delivery in NL because of the paper registration. She''s checking the \"Section 1e\" reference.","signoff":true,"when":{"origin":["NL"],"destZone":["NL"],"type":["B2B"]},"then":{"warning":"","needsVat":true,"level":"ok","entity":"NL","code":"0% NL RC","rate":{"kind":"fixed","value":0},"invoice":"VAT Reversed - Section 1e Dutch Turnover Tax Act (Non-established supplier)"}},{"id":"r-nl-b2c","name":"NL stock to a Dutch consumer","note":"Same 21% as spreadsheet v3, but v3 uses OSS wording for what is a sale within the Netherlands, so the wording says domestic supply.","signoff":false,"when":{"origin":["NL"],"destZone":["NL"],"type":["B2C"]},"then":{"warning":"Standard B2C Rules Apply. Ensure destination address matches consumer location.","needsVat":false,"level":"ok","entity":"NL","code":"Standard NL VAT","rate":{"kind":"dest"},"invoice":"Dutch domestic supply – NL VAT charged at {rate}."}},{"id":"r-other-nl","name":"Other EU stock to a business in NL","note":"Matches spreadsheet v3. Reverse-charged because of the client''s paper NL registration. Miranda is checking the \"Section 1e\" reference.","signoff":true,"when":{"origin":["OTHER"],"destZone":["NL"],"type":["B2B"]},"then":{"warning":"","needsVat":true,"level":"ok","entity":"NL","code":"0% NL RC","rate":{"kind":"fixed","value":0},"invoice":"VAT Reversed - Section 1e Dutch Turnover Tax Act (Non-established supplier)"}},{"id":"r-nonEU-novat","name":"Non-EU customer without a verified EU VAT number","note":"Differs from spreadsheet v3: its tax code says triangulation and its warning tells the user to switch to B2C. Miranda confirmed (13 Oct): without a valid EU VAT number it''s a consumer sale at the delivery country''s rate, so the app does that automatically.","signoff":false,"when":{"origin":["NL","OTHER"],"destZone":["EU"],"type":["B2B"],"custZone":["UK","ROW"],"vies":["unchecked","unavailable"]},"then":{"warning":"The customer is based in {cust} and has no verified EU VAT number, so this is treated as a consumer sale. If they give you a valid {dest} VAT number for the receiving party, check it with VIES: the sale can then be zero-rated.","needsVat":false,"level":"ok","entity":"NL","code":"OSS Destination Rate","rate":{"kind":"dest"},"invoice":"EU OSS B2C Distance Selling – VAT charged at local destination rate for {dest}."}},{"id":"r-triangulation","name":"Triangulation","note":"Differs from spreadsheet v3: its formula still triggers triangulation when the customer''s country differs from the delivery country. Miranda confirmed (14 Oct) it''s when the despatch country, NL and the delivery country are all different. Open point: does it still apply when the customer is based in a different country from the delivery country?","signoff":true,"when":{"origin":["OTHER"],"destZone":["EU"],"type":["B2B"]},"then":{"warning":"There must be exactly one physical cross-border movement of goods. The transport must be arranged and paid for by either the supplier (despatch country) or the intermediary (your business).","needsVat":true,"level":"ok","entity":"NL","code":"0% EU Triangulation","rate":{"kind":"fixed","value":0},"invoice":"VAT Reverse Charge – Simplified Triangulation Rule Applies. Final customer self-accounts for local acquisition VAT."}},{"id":"r-ics","name":"Intra-community supply from NL stock","note":"Differs from spreadsheet v3: its formula calls this triangulation when the customer''s country differs from the delivery country. Goods leaving the Netherlands can''t be triangulation under Miranda''s 14 Oct answer, so this is a plain 0% intra-community supply. Open point: confirm for customers based in a third EU country.","signoff":true,"when":{"origin":["NL"],"destZone":["EU"],"type":["B2B"]},"then":{"warning":"","needsVat":true,"level":"ok","entity":"NL","code":"0% Intra-Community Supply","rate":{"kind":"fixed","value":0},"invoice":"Zero-Rated Intra-Community Supply - Customer accounts for Acquisition VAT in destination country."}},{"id":"r-oss","name":"EU stock to an EU consumer (OSS)","note":"Matches spreadsheet v3.","signoff":false,"when":{"origin":["NL","OTHER"],"destZone":["EU","NL"],"type":["B2C"]},"then":{"warning":"Standard B2C Rules Apply. Ensure destination address matches consumer location.","needsVat":false,"level":"ok","entity":"NL","code":"OSS Destination Rate","rate":{"kind":"dest"},"invoice":"EU OSS B2C Distance Selling – VAT charged at local destination rate for {dest}."}}]'::jsonb, '[{"id":"t01","label":"UK stock to UK business","inp":{"dispatch":"UK","dest":"UK","cust":"UK","type":"B2B","vies":"unchecked","value":"low"},"expect":{"code":"20% UK VAT","rate":20,"entity":"UK"}},{"id":"t02","label":"UK stock to UK consumer","inp":{"dispatch":"UK","dest":"UK","cust":"UK","type":"B2C","vies":"unchecked","value":"low"},"expect":{"code":"20% UK VAT","rate":20,"entity":"UK"}},{"id":"t03","label":"NL stock to the UK, German customer","inp":{"dispatch":"Netherlands","dest":"UK","cust":"Germany","type":"B2B","vies":"unchecked","value":"low"},"expect":{"code":"20% UK VAT","rate":20,"entity":"UK"}},{"id":"t04","label":"French stock to a UK consumer","inp":{"dispatch":"France","dest":"UK","cust":"UK","type":"B2C","vies